                        <!-- Extracted Asset Properties (EXTRACTED ASSETS tab) -->
                        <ScrollViewer x:Name="ExtractedAssetPropertiesPanel" Visibility="Collapsed" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
                            <StackPanel Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,8">
                                    <TextBlock Text="EXTRACTED ASSET PROPERTIES" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                    <TextBlock Text=" ⓘ" FontSize="12" Foreground="#89B4FA" Cursor="Help"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="6,0,0,0"
                                               ToolTipService.InitialShowDelay="0"
                                               ToolTipService.ShowDuration="60000">
                                        <TextBlock.ToolTip>
                                            <ToolTip MaxWidth="420">
                                                <TextBlock TextWrapping="Wrap" Text="EXTRACTED ASSET PROPERTIES — Field Guide&#x0a;&#x0a;─── ASSET METADATA (grey box) ───&#x0a;• Base: The filename (without extension) of the selected sprite.&#x0a;• Folder: Where this sprite lives inside your extracted assets directory.&#x0a;• Extensions: File types found (.act, .spr, .bmp, .pal, etc.).&#x0a;• Suggested: Auto-detected category (ITEM/MONSTER/NPC/CUSTOM) based on folder path.&#x0a;&#x0a;─── ACT/SPR ASSIGNMENT ───&#x0a;• Entity: Choose what kind of game object this sprite is for — ITEM, MONSTER, or NPC. This changes which properties panel appears below and determines the destination folder for sprite installation.&#x0a;• Assign to: Pick an existing database entry (item/monster/NPC) whose sprite files you want to replace or set. The dropdown lists all loaded entries from rAthena's database.&#x0a;• Install related files: When checked, also copies associated .wav, .bmp, and .pal files alongside the .act/.spr.&#x0a;• ASSIGN SPRITE: Copies the sprite files into your client's data folder at the correct path (e.g., data\sprite\item\, data\sprite\몬스터\, data\sprite\npc\).&#x0a;&#x0a;─── ITEM PROPERTIES (Entity=ITEM) ───&#x0a;• Item ID: Unique numeric ID. Custom items typically use 1270000+ range to avoid conflicts with official items.&#x0a;• AegisName: Internal code name used in scripts (max 49 chars, no spaces — use underscores).&#x0a;• Name: Display name shown in-game (max 49 chars).&#x0a;• Type: Item category — determines which fields are valid (Weapon, Armor, etc.).&#x0a;• SubType: Only for Weapon (Dagger/Sword/etc.), Ammo (Arrow/Bullet/etc.), or Card (Normal/Enchant). Ignored for all other types.&#x0a;• Buy/Sell: NPC buy/sell prices in Zeny. If Buy/124 &lt; Sell/75, rAthena forces Sell=1 (exploit prevention).&#x0a;• Weight: Item weight (10 = 1.0 in-game).&#x0a;• Attack/MagicAttack: Physical/magical attack power (Weapon/Ammo only — zeroed for other types).&#x0a;• Defense: Physical defense (Armor/ShadowGear only — zeroed for other types).&#x0a;• Range: Attack range in cells (Weapon only).&#x0a;• Required Lvl / EquipLevelMax: Min/Max character level to equip (0-275). Max must be ≥ Min.&#x0a;• Slots: Card slot count (0-4).&#x0a;• WeaponLevel: Weapon tier 0-5 (Weapon only). ArmorLevel: Armor tier 0-2 (Armor only).&#x0a;• Gender: Both/Male/Female. Musical weapons are forced Male, Whips forced Female by rAthena.&#x0a;• View: Sprite view ID for shields/headgear. AliasName: Reference another item's sprite.&#x0a;• Refineable/Gradable: Whether the item can be refined or graded.&#x0a;• Jobs: Which job classes can equip this item. Check 'All' for universal.&#x0a;• Locations: Equip slot (Head_Top, Armor, etc.). Use Shadow_* slots for ShadowGear type items.&#x0a;• Script: Bonus effects applied while item is equipped (e.g., bonus bStr,10;).&#x0a;• EquipScript/UnEquipScript: Scripts that run once on equip/unequip.&#x0a;• SAVE: Writes the item entry to db/import/item_db.yml on the rAthena server.&#x0a;&#x0a;─── MONSTER PROPERTIES (Entity=MONSTER) ───&#x0a;• Mob ID: Unique monster ID. Custom monsters use ranges above base DB entries.&#x0a;• AegisName: Internal code name (UPPERCASE convention).&#x0a;• Name: Display name shown in-game.&#x0a;• Level/HP/BaseEXP/JobEXP: Core monster stats.&#x0a;• Race/Element/Size: Monster classification affecting damage formulas.&#x0a;• SAVE: Writes to db/import/mob_db.yml.&#x0a;&#x0a;─── NPC PROPERTIES (Entity=NPC) ───&#x0a;• Name: NPC display name.&#x0a;• Sprite ID: Which sprite file to use.&#x0a;• Map: Which map the NPC appears on.&#x0a;• Note: NPC scripts are complex — use ASSIGN SPRITE for the visual, then write the script manually in npc/custom/."/>
                                            </ToolTip>
                                        </TextBlock.ToolTip>
                                    </TextBlock>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <!-- Asset metadata -->
                                <Border Background="#f0f0f0" Padding="8,6" Margin="0,0,0,8" CornerRadius="4">
                                    <StackPanel>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="ExtractedBaseName" Text="Base: —" FontSize="11" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="ExtractedFolder" Text="Folder: —" FontSize="11" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"/>
                                        <TextBlock x:Name="ExtractedExtensions" Text="Extensions: —" FontSize="11"/>
